title: Christien Meindertsma
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
url: https://christienmeindertsma.com/Flax-Chair

Dutch designer. She tends to start with where a material comes from and follow it all the way through.

In 2012 she began the Flax Project and bought one Dutch farm's entire flax harvest, 10 tonnes of it. Then she spent years finding out what could be made from it.

One answer was the [[Flax Chair]] (2015), made with the fiber company [[Enkev]]. Flax fiber and [[PLA]] are pressed into a single panel. The seat is cut and molded from the panel and the leftover becomes the legs.

She doesn't want designers to settle for making "antiques of the future." A thing that lasts still needs a plan for what happens after.

Compare [[Sebastian Cox]], who sells a 10-year guarantee.
